     "text": "Performance Models\n  Performance Is Not Peak FLOPs\n\n¡ Upper Bound: Hardware Throughput\n\n   ¡  Real Performance: Limited by Load Imbalance, Pipeline Efficiency, and Memory Access\n\n\n¡ Speedup of a parallel program\n\n   ¡  P = The number of cores\n\n   ¡  T(1) = Serial running time\n\n   ¡  T(P) = Parallel running time\n\n   ¡  Speedup = T(1) / T(P)\n\n\n¡  Efficiency = Speedup / P\n\n                                        ¡ Speedup and efficiency usually vary with problem\n                                                        size and the number of involved cores",
